# Caddy before Cumino's relay (REL-7): HTTPS for relay.cumino.aleclofabbro.it,
# its certificate from the ACME CAs, renewed by Caddy; every request passed to
# the relay on 127.0.0.1:8080, a collect's NDJSON flushed as it comes
# (`flush_interval -1`, MBX-9). No `log` directive anywhere: Caddy writes no
# access log (CFG-3), only its own faults and its certificates' news, to the
# journal. HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 only: no HTTP/3 offered on a UDP port the
# firewall keeps closed. Installed by provision.sh. [Q, C, 25 Nov 2026]

{
	servers {
		protocols h1 h2
	}
}

relay.cumino.aleclofabbro.it {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
